{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"5a73e7214597509e","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Meditations.md","x":-800,"y":-280,"width":460,"height":400},
		{"id":"eccebe673e2dd805","type":"text","text":"Mortality (Life, urgency, meaningful action/tasks)","x":-1440,"y":260,"width":260,"height":90},
		{"id":"b6764e64fc502c40","type":"text","text":"Control (What you cannot control, what you can)","x":-1620,"y":-380,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cf43d5f856f5b50c","type":"text","text":"[[Dichotomy|Dichotomy of control]] - Divide life into two categories:\n1. What you can control (your emotions, you reactions, how hard you work)\n2. What you cannot control (test results, other peoples’ decisions, money)\n\nAccording to [[Stoicism]] and [[Epictetus]] it is useless to feel sadness when things we cannot control yield a bad result. \nHowever, we can control our responses.\n\nExample\nYou received a test result that you prepared for, it is 57%–a fail. Instead of crying and feeling really sad, you instead work hard to prepare yourself for the next test. \n\nOh wait, this is **exactly** what happened in 2026, start of methods. You got 57% on a test but then on semester 1 exam, you got 91%. That is good improvement. You could control how you reacted. This is exactly what we want in the Dichotomy of control when applying to real life.","x":-2640,"y":-815,"width":800,"height":495},
		{"id":"5998241deeb59af3","type":"text","text":"Aurelius constantly addresses the urgency of mortality. He is aware that we will die very soon, therefore, every [[No action should be undertaken without aim, or other than in conformity with a principle affirming the art of life|action should be meaningful]]. Moreover, we should make the most of **now** by realising our [[Life is a mere fragment of time|mere fragment of time in this universe]] ","x":-2180,"y":231,"width":475,"height":148},
		{"id":"d5b3068cb157f674","type":"text","text":"**Time** \nWe must realise our limited time in this universe\n\n→Complete every task quickly, urgently and amazingly","x":-2550,"y":20,"width":370,"height":200},
		{"id":"c802f69be23cdda3","type":"text","text":"Reality of [[Mortality]]","x":-2600,"y":580,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"6247337abf4b224c","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Life is a mere fragment of time.md","x":-3420,"y":580,"width":460,"height":170},
		{"id":"3bf2c198832f5284","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Amazing and Terrible people inevitably die.md","x":-3360,"y":880,"width":340,"height":270},
		{"id":"741178fe45e0553e","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Nobody will remember you.md","x":685,"y":960,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"1a8d9842a7c4c7b8","type":"text","text":"Cold showers\n\nSimply perform by ‘removing’ the perception of ‘cold’ and you can suddenly do it. Guess what, you are now invincable to cold showers!","x":940,"y":760,"width":500,"height":160},
		{"id":"7b8ad9e6aada277b","type":"text","text":"Perception (pain, embarassment, etc)","x":0,"y":722,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cbef44a539342985","type":"text","text":"**Social**","x":-200,"y":-250,"width":340,"height":50},
		{"id":"93408753f25ac00e","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Remove the judgement 'I am hurt'.md","x":1520,"y":322,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"939869e26c7158db","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Judgement.md","x":885,"y":300,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c6eae15416905df0","type":"text","text":"Meditations strongly encourages us to be respectful of our friends, families, relatives and even enemies. \n\nWe can achieve this by always doing kind actions \n\ne.g. \nmaking brownies\ngiving calls\ndoing the dishwasher/washing machine\ngiving people compliments\n\nliterally anything that makes someone you know feel special. It can even be someone you have never met in your life.","x":240,"y":-454,"width":625,"height":409},
		{"id":"5dc50ed16696b8c8","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Kind to relations (family, friends, etc).md","x":1640,"y":-1140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"4a1af6c64df49027","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/There will always be assholes in the world. Ignore and respect them..md","x":1702,"y":-622,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"68fcee22740f32a2","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Kindness.md","x":1120,"y":-700,"width":220,"height":120},
		{"id":"f058740176e5186c","type":"file","file":"00 Notes/Every hour is meaningful.md","x":-3390,"y":-680,"width":400,"height":400},
